Use one flat formula table so the parser cannot mistake section headings for materials:

```markdown
| # | Ingredient | Dilution | Amount (uL) | Active uL | Active ppm w/w status | Specific function |
|---:|---|---|---:|---:|---|---|
```

Every dilution cell must be `neat`, an explicit `10% w/w`, or an inventory-matching carrier form such as `10% in DPG`; naked percentages are forbidden. Include `**Family archetype:**` and `Concentrate total: 4500 uL`. Mark the volume adapter and finished-matrix omissions explicitly.

